d measurement through the documented CLI + bridge with a real HTTP collector"}, "review_notes": "Fix direction: decide the intent per rule \u2014 if the egress rules are meant to stop exfiltration they must BLOCK (or block-until-approved), not auto-sandbox; if they are meant to contain, then say so plainly in README/specs and stop describing the group as exfil protection. Add an end-to-end regression that runs a local collector and asserts the payload does not arrive for a rule claimed to prevent exfil. Evidence: docs/dogfood/2026-09-18-integration.md \u00a72.4. || TICK 292 VERDICT FOLD: GitReins Tier 2 verdict e158abfa (.gitreins/history/2026-09-19/d22db7f8/verdict.json) PASS \u2014 tier1 PASS + tier2 COMPLETE, all criteria PASS, passed: true, evaluated on commit 9f755906 (the board-close commit; the graded work commit is 3162a25 \u2014 the judge evaluates HEAD at run time). The judge independently re-derived the RED proof (same file -> 4 failed / 2 passed on the pre-fix engine) and independently re-ran the no-delivery E2E (rc=126, collector requests=[], secret delivered: False), the 13 pinned ALLOW controls and 15 upload shapes (failures: 0), the mirror parity probe (ALL PROBES PASS 54/54) and the full suite (821 passed / 5 skipped). || TICK 292 RESTORE (foreman error, disclosed): the board fold commit 4d9952c carried the PRE-FIX bytes of blocklist.py / sandbox.py / 00-builtins.yaml because the Tier-2 judge's RED-proof step had left the worktree holding its temporary revert (its own git-diff check reported clean; the files were not), and the following `git add <three board files>` swept them into the commit. CI run 35419819266 went RED on the reverted tree (the DF-20 tests fail by design against pre-fix code). Fixed forward, not amended: commit 441fec3 restores all three files from the graded work commit 3162a25 (sha256 of blocklist.py identical to 3162a25's; engine probe re-verified block x4 + allow control; parity ALL PROBES PASS; suite 821/5; gitreins guard --full Tier 1 PASS), and CI run 35419873385 on 441fec3 is GREEN. The lesson is recorded in skills/coding-hermes/terminal-jail-foreman-ops (judge leaves source files dirty; prove the tree by hash before any board commit).", "source": "dogfood", "status": "complete", "title": "[dogfood:P1] The egress pack's MODIFY verdicts do not prevent exfiltration \u2014 a real collector received the uploaded secret file (only a BLOCK would)", "ts": "2026-09-18T22:10:40.542868+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-09-18 23:25:00.000000", "worker_status": "complete", "worker_summary": "One worker dispatch, glm-5.3-flash @ zai-glm-default, ~14 min, exit 0, one content commit 3162a25 (+1377/-245, 13 files). The four file-upload egress rules moved from the auto-sandbox layer to the BLOCK layer (builtin-net-curl-upload, -curl-form-upload, -wget-post-file, -remote-tree-copy); blocklist rules are settled by the whole-command pass, so no rewrite and no always-allow short-circuit can approve them. Match-set additions close real bypasses: clustered short flags (-sT, -sd @file, -sF), attached operand -T<path>, =-joined long forms, --data-urlencode name@file, '//' as a whole-tree source, and a quote-aware gap that spans a quoted '&' while still stopping at an unquoted operator. YAML mirror re-baselined to 35 block / 9 sandbox / 10 allow = 54. New end-to-end file plugin/test_egress_no_delivery.py runs the real CLI against a loopback collector: uploads exit 126 with zero requests received; positive controls (plain download, inline-body POST) still execute and still deliver."}
