 {"id": "TJ-GAP-097", "title": "[P1] Resident bridge daemon can hang forever at 100% CPU in accept() after SIGINT/SIGTERM: the signal handler closes the listening socket, then serve()'s `except OSError: continue` turns the closed-fd error into a busy loop — the process never exits and the property test burns its 30s budget waiting on a daemon that is alive and spinning", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "created_at": "2026-10-22T22:38:00-05:00", "created_by": "terminal-jail-foreman", "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "capability_tags": ["resident-bridge", "lifecycle", "signals", "resource-leak"], "complexity": 3, "attempts": 1, "blocked_reason": null, "description": "Observed live during this tick's post-merge full-suite gate on the merged main tree. pytest had been running 9 minutes with only 7s CPU and was blocked in anon_pipe_read; its child /home/kara/terminal-jail/.venv/bin/python plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor_resident.py --serve --sock .../test_sigint_removes_socket0/s.sock had been in state R for 7:47 with 7:45 CPU consumed. py-spy (run as root) showed the main thread inside `accept (socket.py:294)` called from `serve (plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor_resident.py:241)` — i.e. the accept loop, after the signal handler had already closed `server` via _cleanup(). The handler's SystemExit never terminated the process, and the closed fd makes accept() raise OSError on every iteration, so `except OSError: continue` spins forever. Killing the daemon unblocked pytest.", "reasoning": "Found while gating the INT-CI-014 merge (tick terminal-jail-foreman-2026-10-23-02-51-59). Evidence captured on the live process: /proc/<pid>/status 'State: R (running)', Threads 1, SigCgt 0x4002 (SIGINT+SIGTERM caught), 7:45 CPU in 7:47 elapsed; py-spy stack as above. Isolation control: the same 16-trial matrix (idle/mid-stream x SIGTERM/SIGINT, 4 trials each) run standalone with /tmp/tj_signal_spin_probe.py on an idle-ish box exits cleanly 16/16 (rc=143/130, socket removed every time), so the spin needs the loaded full-suite conditions — it is a race, not a deterministic path. Consequence for INT-CI-014: the hosted py3.13 'runner stall' (30s timeout, daemon alive) is very likely THIS spin, not a slow runner, so the retry that INT-CI-014 added is diagnosability only — it does not and must not mask the hang (both attempts still fail on a spinning daemon). Fix direction: make the accept loop exit when the listening socket is gone (EBADF must break/raise, not continue), or have the handler exit the process directly after cleanup, and add a regression test that the daemon is gone within a bounded time after a signal under load.", "detail": {"evidence_run": "tick terminal-jail-foreman-2026-10-23-02-51-59 post-merge gate", "process_state": "State: R (running), Threads: 1, SigCgt: 0000000000004002", "cpu_at_observation": "7:45 CPU / 7:47 elapsed", "py_spy_stack": ["accept (socket.py:294)", "serve (plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor_resident.py:241)", "main (plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor_resident.py:412)"], "isolation_control": "16/16 clean exits standalone (/tmp/tj_signal_spin_probe.py); spin needs full-suite load", "related": ["INT-CI-014", "TJ-REVIEW-073", "INT-CI-012"], "acceptance": ["a signal delivered while the daemon is blocked in accept() exits the process with 128+signum within a bounded time (no busy loop)", "the accept loop cannot spin on a closed listening fd (EBADF breaks/raises rather than continue)", "regression test drives the daemon under load and asserts exit + socket removal within the budget"]}, "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "a623273 (worker) + ce7f0f8 (merge)", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "judge_verdict": "tier2 None / tier1 None — record 61d47549", "worker_summary": "The accept loop no longer treats a closed listening socket as transient: _accept_loop stops on EBADF/fileno()==-1/a set shutdown marker and exits 128+signum, while genuine transient errors still continue. Deterministic regression tests drive the loop with a scripted listener (EBADF stops, EINTR/ECONNABORTED still serves) and fail against the pre-fix loop.", "foreman_note": "Found mid-tick by the post-merge gate, not by a board row: a daemon sat in State R for 7:45 of CPU in 7:47 of wall time after SIGINT, py-spy parked in accept() from serve(), while pytest blocked on its pipe. 16-trial isolation matrix exits clean on an idle box, so the spin needs full-suite load — the fix is structural rather than timing-dependent. The worker disclosed that it could not prove WHY the handler's SystemExit lost the race; the marker covers that window and stderr names it if it ever fires.; orig ci_result: GREEN (run 39901804025 on 30f048d: py3.11/3.12/3.13 + lint + pip-audit + drift guards all success)", "completed_at": "2026-10-22T23:41:35-05:00"}
